==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|is|fjöl|t1=many, multi-|skylda|t2=duty}}, equivalent to {{cog|en|fele}} + {{m|en|shild}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈfjœl.scɪlta/|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|fjölskyldu|fjölskyldur}}

# [[family]]

====Usage notes====
* The term {{m|is|fjölskylda}} was well known in older language referring to many duties or much business with a notion of arduousness rather than the contemporary meaning of “family”. One word used to describe a household or a family unit at the time was {{m|is|hyski}} (once spelled {{m|is|hýski}}).

